[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163586"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082741/assets/5b8ddb36e814517af21d790374e1fb192141bd6ef0fd99e83a147c6ed5a62aea.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{7}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{7}Mr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-0+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31M}{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31M}{35}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ffe23f76-cbf2-5ee1-888a-612dc11574c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" :answer/id #uuid "eff6ed9c-6392-5931-83e1-5eb23d43e9df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609/selection/e9fe03eb46cc37573ec616cc04dc0d03303ea19a17951a98b1d4a181cc97ecac" :answer/id #uuid "682c55f5-e898-5089-86bf-316b20186aea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609/selection/99522c389bf97ae913910ff3f72f66dcbe53251c0f44b1e38c6583e21df32da9" :answer/id #uuid "4b73c887-8008-5c50-ac7e-765248ee1aa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "0c1294f3-f321-5ce1-a4b5-ac0dca8a6fb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63126a26-4cf4-5c06-8d5b-6d0fa87cab70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163609/selection/99522c389bf97ae913910ff3f72f66dcbe53251c0f44b1e38c6583e21df32da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-163609/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-163609/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" "q-163609/selection/e9fe03eb46cc37573ec616cc04dc0d03303ea19a17951a98b1d4a181cc97ecac" "q-163609/selection/99522c389bf97ae913910ff3f72f66dcbe53251c0f44b1e38c6583e21df32da9" "q-163609/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163609" :question/id #uuid "a92867f4-65f2-5f14-8d1b-a73c2c61438b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163609" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=3x,$ $x=1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{M}{45}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{5}+9{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}{\\int }_{1}^{2}12{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}[2{x}^{6}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{45}\\cdot (128-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163609/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613/selection/5350dbb3303540d5ae935fef7f957960d869d647b551207fb2b9b5fdec6dd39e" :answer/id #uuid "e0d0c944-2c09-571a-b932-6ac31ac42186" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer/id #uuid "a101f896-83d8-5acc-833c-86cd9e9bd1e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613/selection/7b4cd2352b8dcfb19000e59d57e4057fae8808d8c274a17c741cc236fceed480" :answer/id #uuid "bcc92b23-4af0-52da-b897-4638f865fb77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613/selection/cbf56d19bccc305869427f7c5238ccc42d3c5697862c48602f3dde94b842f31e" :answer/id #uuid "b1fdf91d-9317-5c37-897f-9ce20e389d68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{20}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613/selection/7b90ad80455272770675a6cc5d2461eafee4c1e9e9d4f5e8dcf9b8b7434b1987" :answer/id #uuid "67ef8e6d-f2f7-5138-befa-944c6d81e56f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "adc80f8e-86ac-5153-8a5b-c59d69c64f30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163613/selection/7b4cd2352b8dcfb19000e59d57e4057fae8808d8c274a17c741cc236fceed480" :answer-field/choices ["q-163613/selection/5350dbb3303540d5ae935fef7f957960d869d647b551207fb2b9b5fdec6dd39e" "q-163613/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" "q-163613/selection/7b4cd2352b8dcfb19000e59d57e4057fae8808d8c274a17c741cc236fceed480" "q-163613/selection/cbf56d19bccc305869427f7c5238ccc42d3c5697862c48602f3dde94b842f31e" "q-163613/selection/7b90ad80455272770675a6cc5d2461eafee4c1e9e9d4f5e8dcf9b8b7434b1987"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163613" :question/id #uuid "ffd0f3a8-7727-507f-bb77-2d0f3f5f20c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163613" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y={x}^{3},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{28M}{3}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}x{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{6}x{y}^{6}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{19}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{20}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7M}{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163613/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "6e6b12e3-d3d4-5fce-9a97-a9d020630dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "7639758c-e2bd-596b-be95-b27cff889761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4fc223e1-2b2d-5ff1-a100-c3dad383b958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654/selection/324ac0c1790f4041f137fa50b4b839fba20ebf09af4d8ea28cd44ee96ed6f4bb" :answer/id #uuid "70ca94a1-c5e0-5434-94ce-6e1a4e93a5c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "f6e243d3-87ac-59be-b10d-d8e8bf871444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "46a5a9ba-52e0-5f87-9e22-f07a2471d91e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163654/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-163654/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-163654/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-163654/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-163654/selection/324ac0c1790f4041f137fa50b4b839fba20ebf09af4d8ea28cd44ee96ed6f4bb" "q-163654/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163654" :question/id #uuid "e271defa-4e74-5933-b22e-63a7dc60b0bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-163654" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 6.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{y}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{6},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}{r}^{5}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot 36\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot 36\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =4M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163654/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658/selection/94dfb22f35fa0e8222d9724a1339e2d5ccff11993402bed8870f2f471afbb3cd" :answer/id #uuid "fd9b8ab3-716b-56da-8d36-7e4c3d570b5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "7e0d77ad-dec6-5384-b919-82727f389e42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c8d59658-59b5-526c-b098-18db77334897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "92328e91-502e-5c01-8430-d0dbd33dc128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658/selection/6e03ecbe0cc56cf8627ed3eb982a5f54d9bde02d09025a256be23be68ab5d8c1" :answer/id #uuid "afdf6637-fbe5-5b35-be94-6ef55e3fc71d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d11cce61-8a3e-51f8-833e-4f95978d8350" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163658/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-163658/selection/94dfb22f35fa0e8222d9724a1339e2d5ccff11993402bed8870f2f471afbb3cd" "q-163658/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-163658/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-163658/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-163658/selection/6e03ecbe0cc56cf8627ed3eb982a5f54d9bde02d09025a256be23be68ab5d8c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163658" :question/id #uuid "72ac20b5-e801-55d9-abc7-3c66cee0c8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163658" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }M\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163658/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
